Stephen Burke VG2 3370 wrote:
> 
> Hi,
> We have some Alpha servers and some Alpha workstations runing DUNIX
> 4.0d.
> 
> We have noticed a little hole with the alpha servers in that you can
> 
> rlogin <HOST> -l root, you get into that server machine as root without
> any passwd being asked for.

/etc/securettys	- if "ptys" lists in this file, root logins are allowed over the
network
/.rhosts	- explicit "allow root rlogin", it lists hosts and user names
		  from which you are allowed access
/etc/hosts.equiv- lists hosts and users that are equivalent to the local users.

Suggestion: empty your /etc/hosts.equiv and check your /.rhosts. Some scripts
may be needing rsh capability, but that is no reason to leave the server wide
open.

Nix.



