From: Nick Wagg <nickw@lsl.co.uk>
Subject: Get CPU speed and total memory
Date: 1999/03/05
Message-ID: <36DFCAF9.411D@lsl.co.uk>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 451533583
Distribution: inet
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 7bit
Followup-To: comp.unix.misc
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=us-ascii
Organization: Laser-Scan Ltd.
Mime-Version: 1.0
Newsgroups: comp.unix.admin,comp.unix.aix,comp.unix.osf.misc,comp.unix.osf.osf1,comp.unix.programmer,comp.unix.questions,comp.unix.solaris

I am trying to write a script which will interrogate the machine on
which it is running for such useful information about:
        CPU speed
        Total memory (RAM)
        Swap space

The idea is that it will be run by someone testing our software and
(s)he will copy the information on to the front of a test script.
This means that it should not require access to privileged commands
or data so, on OSF 1, uerf is out because the system log is protected.
The commands should run from an ordinary shell script which will run
on any machine without having to be installed with special privs either.

Given the nature of the problem, the commands will probably not be
portable but we can cope with that. The platforms I am primarily
interested in are:
        Sun/Solaris
        IBM/AIX
        Alpha/Digital Unix/OSF 1
        HP/HPUX

Suggestions of individual commands, or of widely available and portable
shareware would be most welcome.

TIA
