Hi,

we are trying to run TruCluter/ASE with shared SCSI bus on two
DEC Personal Workstations (one 433au and one 600au). The device
connected via shared SCSI bus is DIGITAL Raid Array 300 (with
HSZ22), the controller in the workstations are KZPSA.

After compiling, modified and rebooted the kernel, the system just
crashes during booting, BEFORE or just at the beginning of loading
and starting ASE.
Only booting the restored (old) kernel works.

We have the same behaviour on both machines, tried with V4.0D and
V4.0E.

Although it is not support by DIGITAL, we heard about that people
are running it in this configuration.

Who knows what to do ? We suggest that some additional kernel modules
are necessary, which normally only loaded on servers.

Please Bcc: your answer to pallo@physnet.uni-hamburg.de

Thanks !

Regards,

Philipp Pallo.




